==English==

===Etymology 1===
{{etyl|la}} {{lena}}, a breaking to pieces, from {{term|frangere|lang=la||to break}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# A [[loud]] and [[sudden]] [[sound]]; the [[report]] of anything [[burst]]ing; a [[crash]].
#* Isaac Watts
#*: The direful '''fragor''', when some southern blast / Tears from the Alps a ridge of knotty oaks{{...}}

===Etymology 2===
By confusion with {{term|fragrant|lang=en}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# {{obsolete|proscribed}} A strong or sweet [[scent]]; [[fragrance]].
#: {{rfquotek|Sir T. Herbert}}

